        "PlanSteelWeightSource": "p.42 items 1 \u002B 4, Pennsylvania girder spans (incl. dams, shoes, walkway, other pay items)",
        "Unresolved": [
          "UNRESOLVED (p.43, p.44): camber of the girders (1 1/4\u0022 spans 1-3, 2\u0022 others, vertical curve) and the girder profile - the girders are cambered for dead load and the vertical curve; the camber diagram gives the maximum only. girders are the straight chord between the W.P.s at their ends on the printed gutter profile (final shape); the profile curve (spans 1-3, up to 3/4\u0022 above the chord) is not followed.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.43, p.44): fixed / expansion end of the girder spans 28-31 - the stress sheet draws the spans with the fixed end away from the river (spans 1-10 fixed at the west end); the same drawing serves spans 28-31. spans 28-31 mirrored: fixed at the EAST end of each span (to be confirmed on sheets 9 / 67 / 68, not read).",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.43, p.44): girder end and bearing position of spans 10 and 28 - p.43 gives the 120\u0027-5 1/4 c-c bearings and \u0027alike except expansion end\u0027 but the floor beam spacing (30\u0027-5 3/4 is for 121\u0027-11) and the end detail are on sheet 9. floor beams at equal spaces of the c-c bearing length (4 spaces), girder ends 1\u0027-1 beyond the bearings, cover plates as spans 1-9.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.46): expansion dams at the piers and the end dams / backwall joints - p.46 dimensions the finger plate dam (edge members 12[ 35, 18 WF 64 diaphragms with 2-Ls 4x4x7/16, anchor bars) but it is a separate pay item. not built; the 4 in. gap between adjacent girder ends is bridged by the slab.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.43): inspection walk (CL 2\u0027-0 from the CL bridge), scuppers, signal / light pole bracket extensions (p.45) - shown on the plan / sections without dimensions I could read. not built.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.44, p.42): service walkway in the girder spans - no walkway sheet for the girder spans was found, but p.42 item 14 lists 2,510 / 1,010 sq ft of grating for them and p.44 mentions floor beam manholes. not built."
        ],
